Why do you care so much about artifacts?  All I ever want artifacts
for are 1) as a decent weapon and 2) as a source of slotless MR.
Sure, half physical damage is *nice*, but if you haven't died before
you get it (especially playing a combat char), you've probably got
enough HP that that's not a major concern.  Branchporting is nice too,
but the Orb will give you virtually the same effect once you have TC.

The artifact 'pool' is no use to you if you can't get at the damn
things.  Chances are that on the one game where you get to the castle
wand unscathed, you'll find Grimtooth and Ogresmasher sitting in the
weapons room, and that damn peaceful Archon over there means
Sunsword's probably been generated too.  So you'll be stuck wishing up
SDSM, speed boots, CoMR and magic markers, like the rest of us.

By playing a lawful character who starts with a long sword, you
virtually *guarantee* an *early* decent artifact weapon.  THIS is what
makes it easier, despite the poor selection of wishable artifacts.  Of
course, mojo is available to all valks, but only if you find an early
altar, or get lucky in minetown.

Artiwishing is extremely rare, in my experience.  If you get lucky in
minetown you can go for the Sceptre, even if you'll never wield the
damn thing.  That's slotless MR sorted, and one fewer ring (conflict)
to polypile for, if you want it*.  Sure, the PYEC and Magicbane are
